# Line endings.
#
# The committed blobs are LF. A Windows working tree is CRLF, and .editorconfig asks for CRLF.
# Without this file git compares the two literally, so every file in the repository shows as
# entirely rewritten and `git diff` becomes useless - which is how a real change hides inside a
# 200-line wall of whitespace during review.
#
# text=auto normalises to LF on the way into the index; eol=crlf checks out CRLF. Nothing about
# the working tree changes, only what git stores and how it compares.
* text=auto eol=crlf

# Anything a shell has to execute needs LF even on Windows, or the interpreter sees a stray CR
# on the shebang line and fails with a message that names a command nobody typed.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Generated and binary. oui.bin is the packed IEEE registry: text=auto guesses well but a wrong
# guess here would silently corrupt a file whose contents nobody eyeballs, and a corrupt vendor
# table shows up as plausible wrong names rather than an error.
*.bin binary
*.pcap binary
*.pcapng binary
*.db binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
